ll put that in config_level. I think matrix_tables + config_level is defensible.\n\nHmm, actually let me reconsider once more. Could I do model_level with model = \"EMT-Lx DN50 G100\" style for qmax/qt/qmin only? It would be 3 attributes × 78 models. That's a lot of JSON but systematic. The risk: extremely long output. Given no strict length limit, but practical limits, I'll skip and rely on matrix_tables. The schema says matrix_tables is for \"multi-dim tables that don't fit elsewhere\" — this fits that escape hatch.\n\nNow write out expanded rows.\n\n**Page 3 Table 1 expanded rows:**\n\nRow 1 (EMT-Lx or EMT-Dc, DN body 50, DN cartr 80, std bearings 3x6x3 front / 2x5x2 rear, opt 3x8x4 front / 3x6x3 rear, drums 7/1, control 0.02):\n- v1: G100, Qmax160, Qt32, Qmin20:8, Qmin30:5, Qmin50:3, blade 55, qty 12\n- v2: G160, Qmax250, Qt50, Qmin 12.5, 8, 5, blade 45, qty 14\n- v3: G250, Qmax400, Qt80, Qmin 20, 12.5, 8, blade 35, qty 16\n\nRow 2 (all four types, DN 80/80, same bearings as row1, drums 7/1, control 0.02):\n- G100: 160/32/8,5,3; 55; 12\n- G160: 250/50/12.5,8,5; 45; 14\n- G250: 400/80/20,12.5,8; 35; 16\n\nRow 3 (EMT-Lx/Dc, DN 80/100, bearings std 3x8x4/3x6x3, opt 5x10x3/3x6x3, drums 7/1, control 0.02):\n- G160: Qmax250, Qt50, Qmin 12.5/8/5; 55; 12\n- G250: 400/80/20/12.5/8; 45; 14\n- G400: 650/130/32.5/20/12.5; 35; 16\n\nRow 4 (EMT-Lx/Dc, DN 100/80, same as row1 bearings, drums 7/1, 0.02):\n- G100: 160, 32, 8/5/3; 55; 12\n- G160: 250, 50, 12.5/8/5; 45; 14\n- G250: 400, 80, 20/12.5/8; 35; 16\n\nRow 5 (all four, DN 100/100, bearings as row3, drums 7/1, 0.02):\n- G160: 250, 50, 12.5/8/5; 55; 12\n- G250: 400, 80, 20/12.5/8; 45; 14\n- G400: 650, 130, 32.5/20/12.5; 35; 16\n\nRow 6 (EMT-Lx/Dc, DN 100/150, bearings 5x11x5/5x11x5 std, 5x16x5/5x11x5 opt, drums 7/1 or 8/0, control 0.02 or 0.2):\n- G400: 650, 130, 32.5/20/12.5; 55; 12\n- G650: 1000, 200, 50/32/20; 45; 14\n- G1000: 1600, 320, 80/50/32; 35; 16\n\nRow 7 (EMT-Lx/Dc, DN 150/100, bearings 3x8x4/3x6x3, opt 5x10x3/3